   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Dear\nlist,</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I\nam working in R with detection functions (using Distance package). I\nhave selected a hazar-rate key function with size group as covariable, as\nthis:</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size&lt;-ds(distaire,\ntruncation = &quot;5%&quot;, formula= ~size, key=&quot;hr&quot;,\nadjustment=NULL).</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\">\n</font><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">There\nare some rounding problems with data, so I would like to adjust\nintervals in order to correct them, using this code:</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">cutpts\n&lt;- seq(0, 719, length=7)  # w = 719</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size.bin&lt;-ds(distaire,\nkey=&quot;hr&quot;, formula= ~size, adjustment=NULL, cutpoints =\ncutpts)</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">But\nthis message appears:</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Fitting\nhazard-rate key function</font></font></font></i></p><i>\n</i><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">All\nmodels failed to fit!</font></font></font></i></p><i>\n</i><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Error\nin ds(distaire, key = &quot;hr&quot;, formula = ~size, adjustment =\nNULL,  : </font></font></font></i>\n</p><i>\n</i><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\">\n <font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">No models could be\nfitted.</font></font></font></i></p><i>\n</i><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">In\naddition: Warning message:</font></font></font></i></p><i>\n</i><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">In\ncreate.bins(data, cutpoints) :</font></font></font></i></p><i>\n</i><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\">\n <font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Some distances were\noutside bins and have been removed</font></font></font></i></p><i>\n</i><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I&#39;ve\ntried with this:</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size.bin&lt;-ds(distaire,\nkey=&quot;hr&quot;, formula= ~size, adjustment=NULL, cutpoints =\nc(0,114,228,342,456,570,684,719) )</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">And\nthe same problem arises</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I\nhave tried with half-normal function and it works...</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">The\nstrange thing to me is that several days ago I had no problems with\nthis code, I could fit models without problem; the only thing I did\nin the middle was update R... </font></font></font>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Any\nhelp I&#39;ll really appreciate</font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Best regards<br></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Natalia</font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\"><br></font></font></font></p>\n</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
