   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    <p>Natalia</p>\r\n    <p>Indeed a mystery--most disconcerting that you report the problem\r\n      occurs when fitting one key function but not the other key\r\n      function.  My suspicion is that with 5% truncation the truncation\r\n      width might not be precisely 719 as you suspect.<br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>The best way to resolve the mystery is for you to send along\r\n      either an RData file containing the data object &quot;distaire&quot; or the\r\n      data file to my email address.<br>\r\n    </p></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>On 16/09/2016 01:21, Natalia wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      \r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Dear\r\n                list,</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I\r\n                am working in R with detection functions (using Distance\r\n                package). I\r\n                have selected a hazar-rate key function with size group\r\n                as covariable, as\r\n                this:</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size&lt;-ds(distaire,\r\n                truncation = &quot;5%&quot;, formula= ~size, key=&quot;hr&quot;,\r\n                adjustment=NULL).</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\">\r\n          </font><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">There\r\n                are some rounding problems with data, so I would like to\r\n                adjust\r\n                intervals in order to correct them, using this code:</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">cutpts\r\n                &lt;- seq(0, 719, length=7) # w = 719</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size.bin&lt;-ds(distaire,\r\n                key=&quot;hr&quot;, formula= ~size, adjustment=NULL, cutpoints =\r\n                cutpts)</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">But\r\n                this message appears:</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Fitting\r\n                  hazard-rate key function</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n        <i>\r\n        </i>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">All\r\n                  models failed to fit!</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n        <i>\r\n        </i>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Error\r\n                  in ds(distaire, key = &quot;hr&quot;, formula = ~size,\r\n                  adjustment =\r\n                  NULL, : </font></font></font></i>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <i>\r\n        </i>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"> <font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">No models could be\r\n                  fitted.</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n        <i>\r\n        </i>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">In\r\n                  addition: Warning message:</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n        <i>\r\n        </i>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">In\r\n                  create.bins(data, cutpoints) :</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n        <i>\r\n        </i>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"> <font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Some distances were\r\n                  outside bins and have been removed</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n        <i>\r\n        </i>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I&#39;ve\r\n                tried with this:</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size.bin&lt;-ds(distaire,\r\n                key=&quot;hr&quot;, formula= ~size, adjustment=NULL, cutpoints =\r\n                c(0,114,228,342,456,570,684,719) )</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">And\r\n                the same problem arises</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I\r\n                have tried with half-normal function and it works...</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">The\r\n                strange thing to me is that several days ago I had no\r\n                problems with\r\n                this code, I could fit models without problem; the only\r\n                thing I did\r\n                in the middle was update R... </font></font></font>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n        </p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Any\r\n                help I&#39;ll really appreciate</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Best regards<br>\r\n              </font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Natalia</font></font></font></p>\r\n        <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\"><br>\r\n              </font></font></font></p>\r\n      </div></blockquote></div>"
