  {
   "id": "0zJKOm8OAwAJ",
   "from": "Natalia Schroeder",
   "author": "8753e7ce2213ca31",
   "date": "2016-09-20T21:01:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] error message with hazard rate function and cutpoints",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div>Hi Eric,<br>Thanks so much to you and David, the code works now.<br>Regarding to your observation of the &#39;bump&#39; in the histogram, we think it&#39;s a noise in the data (maybe it was easier to detect animals from the aircraft to that distance). We trust correcting the bump with the distribution of intervals.<br></div>Thanks again!<br></div>Natalia<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2016-09-19 1:05 GMT-07:00 Eric Rexstad <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">er...@st-andrews.ac.uk</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\">\r\n    <p>Natalia</p>\r\n    <p>Thanks to the fast coding of Dave Miller, the bug that prevented\r\n      your fitting of a hazard rate key function model to your binned\r\n      data has been resolved.</p>\r\n    <p>The trouble resided in the mrds package, so Dave has patched\r\n      mrds.  To install this version of mrds, issue these commands:</p>\r\n    <p><tt>library(devtools)</tt><tt><br>\r\n      </tt><tt>install_github(&quot;DistanceDevelopment/mrds&quot;)</tt></p>\r\n    <p>You can then proceed to install the Distance package you already\r\n      have and run the ds() function in this manner</p>\r\n    <p><tt>hr.5pct.bins &lt;- ds(data=natalia, key=&quot;hr&quot;, truncation =\r\n        719, </tt><tt><br>\r\n      </tt><tt>                   cutpoints = seq(from=0, to=719,\r\n        length.out = 7))</tt><br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p>to produce</p>\r\n    <p><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/30e6f3a4a32d3/fpnghifnjaapikdg.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" alt=\"\"></p>\r\n    In my opinion, you need to understand why you have the bump in your\r\n    detections between 500 and 600m.  This hazard rate model with cosine\r\n    adjustments is trying to accommodate that bump--is it noise in the\r\n    data, or a process that causes this?  You can judge whether it might\r\n    be preferable to smooth through that bump with a half normal model.<div><div><br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>On 16/09/2016 09:12, Eric Rexstad\r\n      wrote:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    </div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div>\r\n      \r\n      <p>Natalia</p>\r\n      <p>Indeed a mystery--most disconcerting that you report the\r\n        problem occurs when fitting one key function but not the other\r\n        key function.  My suspicion is that with 5% truncation the\r\n        truncation width might not be precisely 719 as you suspect.<br>\r\n      </p>\r\n      <p>The best way to resolve the mystery is for you to send along\r\n        either an RData file containing the data object &quot;distaire&quot; or\r\n        the data file to my email address.<br>\r\n      </p>\r\n      <br>\r\n      <div>On 16/09/2016 01:21, Natalia wrote:<br>\r\n      </div>\r\n      </div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\" text=\"#000000\"><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n        <div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Dear list,</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I am working in R with detection functions\r\n                  (using Distance package). I have selected a hazar-rate\r\n                  key function with size group as covariable, as this:</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size&lt;-ds(distaire, truncation = &quot;5%&quot;,\r\n                  formula= ~size, key=&quot;hr&quot;, adjustment=NULL).</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"> </font><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">There are some rounding problems with data,\r\n                  so I would like to adjust intervals in order to\r\n                  correct them, using this code:</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">cutpts &lt;- seq(0, 719, length=7) # w = 719</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size.bin&lt;-ds(distaire, key=&quot;hr&quot;,\r\n                  formula= ~size, adjustment=NULL, cutpoints = cutpts)</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">But this message appears:</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Fitting hazard-rate key function</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n          <i> </i>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">All models failed to fit!</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n          <i> </i>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Error in ds(distaire, key = &quot;hr&quot;, formula =\r\n                    ~size, adjustment = NULL, : </font></font></font></i>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <i> </i>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"> <font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">No models could be fitted.</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n          <i> </i>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">In addition: Warning message:</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n          <i> </i>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">In create.bins(data, cutpoints) :</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n          <i> </i>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><i><font color=\"#000000\"> <font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Some distances were outside bins and have\r\n                    been removed</font></font></font></i></p>\r\n          <i> </i>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I&#39;ve tried with this:</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">hr.size.bin&lt;-ds(distaire, key=&quot;hr&quot;,\r\n                  formula= ~size, adjustment=NULL, cutpoints =\r\n                  c(0,114,228,342,456,570,684,719) )</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">And the same problem arises</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">I have tried with half-normal function and it\r\n                  works...</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">The strange thing to me is that several days\r\n                  ago I had no problems with this code, I could fit\r\n                  models without problem; the only thing I did in the\r\n                  middle was update R... </font></font></font> </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><br>\r\n          </p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Any help I&#39;ll really appreciate</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Best regards<br>\r\n                </font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\">Natalia</font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:200%\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Times New Roman, serif\"><font size=\"3\"><br>\r\n                </font></font></font></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n        -- <br>\r\n        You received this message because you are subscribed to the\r\n        Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.<br></blockquote></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
